---
description: Localize first semantic divergences by lineage and discriminating probe contributions.
args:
  context: InvestigationContext
  state: InvestigationState
returns: Diagnosis
---
1. For each supported hypothesis trace its source DefinitionLinks from target question to the selected
   implementation role. Identify the first incompatible meaning, not merely the downstream output label.
2. Combine explicit source contrast with actual probe outcome and changed intermediate plan fields.
   A source difference without any discriminating probe remains unexercised; an unexplained numeric gap
   without source meaning remains unresolved.
3. Build RootCauses with dimension, exact definitionIds, contrastId, supporting probeIds, reason and
   source witnesses. Preserve separate population, anchor and metric causes when each is exercised.
4. Do not force all mismatches into one earliest global stage. Different branches can diverge independently,
   then compensate at a later aggregate; first means earliest on the relevant directed lineage path.
5. Record coincidences where baseline figures agree despite these different meanings. Name the
   compensating composition and its observed numerator/denominator evidence rather than a vague chance label.
6. Preserve unresolved hypotheses and failed probe premises with exact IDs. Exhaustion does not
   promote a merely possible mechanism to a supported root cause.
7. Return rootCauses, coincidences and unresolved. The repair stage consumes these affected definition
   identities and must leave source-equivalent roles untouched.
8. Every root-cause entry needs both a source-bound contrast and a materialized intervention witness.
   Call depth or a confident explanation alone is insufficient localization evidence.
